Summary of modifications in this project. The nucleosome-profiling stage is a
deliberate architectural reimplementation; see
COMPARISON.md for the labelled, evidence-backed record of every change (which
divergences are intended vs. bugs, and their validation).

Stage 1 — GC correction (gc_correction/):
  - griffin_GC_counts_prefixsum.py: prefix-sum rewrite of Griffin's GC counting.
    Builds a per-chromosome cumulative-GC array once (O(1) per-fragment GC via
    array subtraction, no per-fragment reference fetch), with an exact seeded
    fallback for ambiguous IUPAC bases so results stay BIT-IDENTICAL to the
    original. Per-chromosome parallelism.
  - griffin_GC_bias.py: replaced removed pandas .append with pd.concat (output
    unchanged); added an optional --no_plots flag and a headless-safe matplotlib
    backend; smoothing unchanged.

Stage 2 — nucleosome profiling (nucleosome_profiling/), all Griffin-derived:
  - 02_fcc_count.sh: GC-corrected midpoint (FCC) counting as a genome-wide track
    (vs Griffin's per-site coverage), sparse output. Derived from griffin_coverage.
  - 04_profile_tf_sites.py: slices +/-5 kb windows around TFBS from the FCC track
    and bins to 15 bp. Derived from griffin_merge_sites.
  - 04_merge_and_extract.py: outlier mask -> composite -> smooth -> normalize ->
    feature extraction. Derived from griffin_merge_sites.
  See COMPARISON.md for the full stage-by-stage mapping, intended divergences,
  fixed bugs, and validation (including external validation vs Griffin on CDX2).

Pipeline / orchestration (not derived from Griffin; original to this project):
  - run_all.sh, gc_correction/run_gc_correction.sh,
    nucleosome_profiling/run_profiling.sh: plain-bash drivers (no Snakemake/SLURM).
  - build_stage2_sheet.py, nucleosome_profiling/config_helper.py: the
    Stage-1 -> Stage-2 seam (gc_correction_manifest.tsv -> samples.tsv) and the
    config/sheet reader.
  - environment.yml: single consolidated runtime environment.

The active Stage-1 -> Stage-2 handoff is the gc_correction_manifest.tsv -> build_stage2_sheet.py -> samples.tsv seam.